tatus bool }`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd074-sha224sum.yaml**\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1-R4, goals G1-G3, non-goals, package contract, and acceptance criteria\n     - Key: R3 (binary/text/tag mode flags) and R4 (exit codes and SIGPIPE) are the target requirements\n     - Non-goals: no HMAC-SHA224, no SHA-256 computation\n   \n   - **cmd/sha224sum/main.go** (existing, 172 lines)\n     - Already contains a complete implementation with all flag parsing, check mode, digest mode\n     - Important: The existing code ALREADY appears to implement R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2 through delegation to pkg/hashutil\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bytes\"\n         \"crypto/sha256\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     // [helpText and versionText constants omitted for brevity]\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n             Algorithm: \"SHA224\",\n             NewHash:   sha256.New224,\n             DigestLen: 28,\n         }\n         var stdout io.Writer = os.Stdout\n         if opts.zero {\n             stdout = &nulWriter{w: os.Stdout}\n         }\n         if opts.check {\n             checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{\n                 Warn:   opts.warn,\n                 Quiet:  opts.quiet,\n                 Status: opts.status,\n             }\n             exitCode := 0\n             for _, f := range files {\n                 ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, stdout, os.Stderr)\n                 if err != nil {\n                