{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018CPJyaEjsanJ3dw1yMFsFj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The existing `cmd/sha224sum/main.go` already fully implements all four requirements:\n\n- **R3.1**: `-b`/`--binary` sets `opts.binary = true`, `-t`/`--text` sets `opts.binary = false` (default). Both are passed to `hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, ...)` which handles the `\"HASH *FILENAME\"` vs `\"HASH  FILENAME\"` formatting.\n- **R3.2**: `--tag` sets `opts.tag = true`, passed to `hashutil.DigestFiles` which produces BSD tag format `\"SHA224 (FILENAME) = HASH\"` regardless of binary/text mode.\n- **R4.1**: `DigestFiles` returns 0 on success → `os.Exit(0)`. `VerifyChecksums` returning `(true, nil)` keeps `exitCode = 0` → `os.Exit(0)`.\n- **R4.2**: `DigestFiles` returns 1 on file errors → `os.Exit(1)`. `VerifyChecksums` returning `(false, _)` or `(_, err)` sets `exitCode = 1` → `os.Exit(1)`.\n\nNo modifications are needed. The implementation compiles without errors and passes `go vet`. All R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2 logic is correctly delegated to `pkg/hashutil` with no duplicated checksum logic in `cmd/sha224sum/main.go`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":25272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a925d3d5-021e-46a4-a52c-4f5f483e948f","uuid":"2a6a2074-f3e1-4592-9707-d97cc80663ee"}
